   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Your kubectl apply just changed more than you thought."
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Apply does not show you a preview first."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "Hand edits, drift, or the wrong context, and you find out in production."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Run kubectl diff first. The API server previews what apply would change. Exit code zero, no differences. Exit code one, differences found. Gate CI on it, then apply."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "Diff first, or straight to apply? Comment which one your team does."
  },
  {
   "id": "follow",
   "text": "Follow me for one DevOps fix every day."
